{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following MS C++ code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original MS C++ code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <cmath>\n#include <cstdlib>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint gcd(int a, int b) {\n    return b == 0 ? a : gcd(b, a % b);\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int x, y, limit;\n    scanf(\"%d%d%d\", &x, &y, &limit);\n    double bestDist = 1e9;\n    double target = (double)x / y;\n    int bestNum = 0, bestDen = 0;\n    for (int i = 1; i <= limit; ++i) {\n        long long b = (1LL * x * i) / y;\n        int cand[3];\n        cand[0] = (int)b;\n        cand[1] = abs((int)b - 1);\n        cand[2] = (int)b + 1;\n        for (int j = 0; j < 3; ++j) {\n            double approx = (double)cand[j] / i;\n            double dist = fabs(target - approx);\n            if (dist < bestDist) {\n                bestDist = dist;\n                bestNum = cand[j];\n                bestDen = i;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    double distOne = fabs(1.0 - target);\n    double distBest = fabs((double)bestNum / bestDen - target);\n    if (distOne <= distBest + 1e-9) {\n        bestNum = 1;\n        bestDen = 1;\n    }\n    int g = gcd(bestNum, bestDen);\n    printf(\"%d/%d\\n\", bestNum / g, bestDen / g);\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\nimport math\n\ndef gcd(a, b):\n    return math.gcd(a, b)\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().strip().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    x, y, limit = map(int, data[:3])\n    target = x / y\n    best_dist = 1e9\n    best_num = 0\n    best_den = 0\n    for i in range(1, limit + 1):\n        b = (x * i) // y\n        candidates = [b, abs(b - 1), b + 1]\n        for cand in candidates:\n            approx = cand / i\n            dist = abs(target - approx)\n            if dist < best_dist:\n                best_dist = dist\n                best_num = cand\n                best_den = i\n    dist_one = abs(1.0 - target)\n    dist_best = abs(best_num / best_den - target)\n    if dist_one <= dist_best + 1e-9:\n        best_num = 1\n        best_den = 1\n    g = gcd(best_num, best_den)\n    print(f\"{best_num // g}/{best_den // g}\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n1.0\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.9409251809120178, -0.0003300360403954983, -6.437280717364047e-06, 0.0, 0.0, -9.715084888739511e-05, -0.00038413776201196015, -0.03804141283035278, -0.015069803223013878, -0.004079354461282492, 0.0, -0.00010072677832795307, -4.994744449504651e-05, -0.6038804650306702, -6.556489552167477e-06, -0.0032238198909908533, 0.0, -9.298280929215252e-06, -5.960462772236497e-07, -0.02340872399508953, -0.030285686254501343, 0.0, 0.0, -0.0002051381452474743, -3.576278118089249e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.006737136282026768, -0.0031894787680357695, -0.00043072958942502737, -8.34461570775602e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.010758139193058014, 0.0, -6.985420623095706e-05, 0.0, -0.011047860607504845, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.005233872216194868, -7.867782187531702e-06, -1.7881377516459906e-06, -1.4305104514278355e-06,